\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{What verifiability certifies}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{rlvr}
\tag{verifier}

\p{Verifiability certifies that a declared procedure can reproduce evidence
and a decision. It does not certify that the checked predicate equals the full
task objective. An answer checker may ignore reasoning. A unit-test suite may
omit relevant behavior. A sandbox may expose an unintended shortcut.}

\p{DeepSeek-R1's rule rewards in
\citet{Section 2.2.2}{guo2025deepseek} make the checked predicates explicit.
DAPO's reward and sampling interventions in
\citet{Section 3}{yu2025dapo} show that optimizer behavior also depends on
which samples enter the update. Neither source proves that a verifier is a
complete evaluator.}

\p{The immediate theorem questions are local. How do false positives alter
the expected advantage? When does group normalization erase a rare signal?
Which support conditions prevent clipping from hiding useful responses? Each
question requires a verifier model and an independent evaluation criterion.}
